    <md:uuid>eb95f103-8cae-435b-b534-3f93377dd37a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will find the solutions to systems of linear inequalities in two variables.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Write a system of inequalities to describe a situation, find the solution by graphing, and interpret points in the solution.</item>
  <item>Explain what is meant by “the solutions to a system of inequalities” and describe the graphs that represent the solutions.</item>
  <item>Find values that satisfy each constraint individually, and values that satisfy both constraints at once, when given descriptions and graphs that represent two different constraints. </item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item>2.14.1: Modeling Equations to Solve a Riddle</item>
  <item>2.14.2: Finding a Pair of Values that Satisfies Multiple Inequalities</item><list>
  <item>2.14.2: Self Check</item>
  <item>2.14.2: Additional Resources</item></list>

  <item>2.14.3: Writing Systems of Inequalities that Represent Situations</item><list>
  <item>2.14.3: Self Check</item>
  <item>2.14.3: Additional Resources</item></list>

  <item>2.14.4: Graphing Solutions of Systems of Inequalities</item>
  <item>2.14.5: Writing Inequalities for Situations and Representing on a Graph</item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item>2.14.6: Practice</item>
  <item>2.14.7: Lesson Summary</item>
</list>
 </section>
